{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794734515,"nonce":"pOAaBALLodYuJrgvCT+dwweEpUU=","title":"Test D1 migrations against non-empty, realistic data","message":"Migrations are only partly tested against existing rows:\n\n- api/src/migrations.test.ts applies one migration to rows inserted by hand, on node:sqlite in memory. Only 0007 and 0011 (#89) have such a test; 0001-0006 and 0008-0010 don't, including 0005, which rebuilt a table.\n- The workerd tests apply every migration to an empty local D1 (src/testing/harness.ts:64, applyD1Migrations), so a migration's data-moving statements run on no rows there.\n\nNot covered:\n- A migration run on D1 (miniflare) with data in it: D1 enforces foreign keys, and table renames rewrite references, which a rebuild like 0011's relies on.\n- A migration run on realistic data: nothing applies pending migrations to a copy of staging or production.\n\nOptions:\n- A workerd test that seeds rows at the schema before a migration, then applies the rest, as migrations.test.ts does in node:sqlite. Needs applying migrations one at a time in the harness.\n- A check that exports staging's D1 (wrangler d1 export, read-only), applies the pending migrations to it locally, and compares row counts and key columns before and after. Could run in CI on PRs that add a migration.\n\nPrompted by 0011 (attribution table, #89): its copies into the rebuilt user_document and user_document_annotation use an inner JOIN to attribution, so an unmatched row would be dropped silently rather than fail.","files":null}]}